---
import "../../styles/global.css";

const canonicalURL = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site);
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Keesing Puzzle Hunt — Terms and Conditions</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Terms and conditions for participation in the Keesing Puzzle Hunt."
    />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalURL} />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=Source+Serif+4:opsz,wght@8..60,500;8..60,600&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
  </head>

  <body>
    <main>
      <article class="legal-page site-container">
        <header class="legal-header">
          <h1>Keesing Puzzle Hunt — Terms and Conditions</h1>
          <p class="last-updated"><strong>Last updated: October 8, 2026</strong></p>
        </header>

        <div class="legal-content">
          <p>
            These Terms and Conditions (“Terms”) govern participation in the
            Keesing Puzzle Hunt (“Hunt”), including use of its SMS
            text-messaging service. By enrolling in or participating in the
            Hunt, you agree to these Terms.
          </p>

          <h2>1. About the Hunt</h2>

          <p>
            The Keesing Puzzle Hunt is a voluntary, interactive puzzle game.
            Participants solve clues, travel to locations, and may use SMS text
            messaging to receive instructions, clues, and feedback.
          </p>

          <p>
            Some activities allow participants to voluntarily send their
            location from a mobile phone. The Hunt may use that location to
            calculate distance from a target and provide feedback such as
            WARMER or COLDER.
          </p>

          <p>
            The Hunt is owned and operated by Ron Keesing as a sole proprietor
            and is currently developed as a personal, volunteer-developed
            project.
          </p>

          <h2>2. Adult Enrollment Required</h2>

          <p>
            Each team must be enrolled by a person who is at least 18 years old
            (“Enrolling Adult”).
          </p>

          <p>By texting JOIN, the Enrolling Adult confirms that they:</p>

          <ul>
            <li>Are at least 18 years old;</li>
            <li>
              Have read and agree to these Terms and the Hunt Privacy Policy;
            </li>
            <li>
              Consent to receive automated SMS messages associated with
              participation in the Hunt; and
            </li>
            <li>
              Accept responsibility for appropriately supervising minors
              participating as members of their team.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            Minors may participate as members of a team but may not
            independently enroll a team. Minors should participate under
            appropriate adult supervision.
          </p>

          <h2>3. SMS Consent and Communications</h2>

          <p>
            To enroll a team, the Enrolling Adult texts JOIN to the designated
            Keesing Puzzle Hunt telephone number.
          </p>

          <p>
            By texting JOIN, the Enrolling Adult expressly consents to receive
            automated text messages necessary to operate the Hunt. These may
            include enrollment confirmations, instructions, clues,
            location-based responses, and other messages directly related to
            participation.
          </p>

          <p>
            Consent to receive messages is not a condition of purchasing any
            goods or services. The Hunt does not use enrollment in the SMS
            service to send advertising or promotional messages.
          </p>

          <p>
            Message frequency varies depending primarily on participant
            activity. Participants generally receive messages in response to
            messages or locations they submit.
          </p>

          <p>Message and data rates may apply.</p>

          <h2>4. Stopping Messages</h2>

          <p>
            Participants may cancel SMS participation at any time by texting
            STOP to the Hunt telephone number.
          </p>

          <p>
            After STOP is received, no further Hunt messages will be sent except
            for messages necessary to confirm or administer the opt-out, as
            permitted or required by the messaging service or wireless carrier.
          </p>

          <p>
            A participant who later wishes to participate again may need to
            text START before enrolling again.
          </p>

          <h2>5. Help</h2>

          <p>Text HELP to the Hunt telephone number for instructions and assistance.</p>

          <p>
            Additional assistance is available at:<br />
            <a href="mailto:ron@keesingai.com">ron@keesingai.com</a>
          </p>

          <h2>6. Location Information</h2>

          <p>
            Some Hunt activities ask participants to voluntarily share a
            location from their mobile device.
          </p>

          <p>
            The Hunt does not continuously track participants and does not have
            access to a participant's device location unless the participant
            affirmatively sends location information.
          </p>

          <p>
            When a location is submitted, the Hunt may use its latitude and
            longitude to calculate the participant's distance from a target and
            determine whether the participant is moving closer to or farther
            from it.
          </p>

          <p>
            The Hunt application is designed not to retain a history of
            submitted locations. After calculating distance, the application
            retains only the game state necessary to provide subsequent
            feedback, such as the previously calculated distance from the
            target.
          </p>

          <p>
            Additional information about data handling is contained in the Hunt
            Privacy Policy:<br />
            <a href="/hunt/privacy/">https://keesingai.com/hunt/privacy/</a>
          </p>

          <h2>7. Participant Safety and Responsibility</h2>

          <p>
            Participation in the Hunt is voluntary. Participants are
            responsible for determining whether they can safely undertake any
            activity associated with the Hunt.
          </p>

          <p>
            Participants must exercise reasonable care and good judgment at all
            times. Participants must:
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>Obey applicable laws, traffic signals, signs, and posted restrictions;</li>
            <li>
              Remain on public property or other property they are authorized
              to enter;
            </li>
            <li>
              Avoid roadways, restricted areas, hazardous locations, and other
              unsafe situations;
            </li>
            <li>
              Never interpret a clue as an instruction to trespass or undertake
              an unsafe or unlawful activity;
            </li>
            <li>
              Remain aware of traffic, terrain, weather, other people, and
              surrounding conditions;
            </li>
            <li>
              Not use a mobile device while driving or whenever doing so would
              create a safety hazard; and
            </li>
            <li>
              Provide appropriate adult supervision for minors participating on
              their team.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            If a clue, location, or instruction appears unsafe, participants
            should not proceed.
          </p>

          <h2>8. Assumption of Risk</h2>

          <p>
            Participants acknowledge that the Hunt may involve walking,
            navigating public spaces, crossing streets, encountering uneven or
            slippery surfaces, exposure to traffic and weather, and other risks
            ordinarily associated with outdoor recreational activities.
          </p>

          <p>
            Participants voluntarily choose whether and how to participate and
            acknowledge and assume the risks they knowingly encounter and
            accept in doing so.
          </p>

          <p>
            The Enrolling Adult is responsible for exercising appropriate
            judgment concerning participation by minors on their team and for
            providing appropriate supervision.
          </p>

          <h2>9. GPS, Clue, and Service Accuracy</h2>

          <p>
            GPS positions, calculated distances, maps, clues, directions, and
            other information provided through the Hunt may be approximate,
            delayed, incomplete, or inaccurate.
          </p>

          <p>
            Participants must use their own observations and judgment and must
            not rely upon the Hunt, GPS information, or SMS responses when
            making safety-related decisions.
          </p>

          <p>
            The Hunt may also be interrupted or unavailable because of cellular
            coverage, internet connectivity, device limitations,
            telecommunications delays, software errors, or other technical
            problems.
          </p>

          <p>Mobile carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages.</p>

          <h2>10. Limitation of Liability</h2>

          <p>
            To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, the Hunt's
            operator, organizers, and volunteers will not be liable for
            indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or similar damages
            arising from participation in the Hunt or use or inability to use
            the Hunt's SMS or location-based services, including damages
            resulting from interrupted service, delayed messages, inaccurate
            GPS information, technical errors, or loss of data.
          </p>

          <p>
            Nothing in these Terms is intended to exclude, waive, or limit any
            liability that cannot lawfully be excluded, waived, or limited under
            applicable law.
          </p>

          <h2>11. Privacy and Use of Participant Information</h2>

          <p>
            The Hunt is designed to minimize the collection and retention of
            personal information.
          </p>

          <p>
            Information collected or processed through the SMS service is used
            only as necessary to operate, maintain, secure, and troubleshoot the
            Hunt.
          </p>

          <p>
            The Hunt does not sell participant information and does not share or
            disclose participants' mobile telephone numbers, SMS opt-in
            information, or consent to third parties for advertising or
            marketing purposes.
          </p>

          <p>
            Service providers, including telecommunications and internet
            infrastructure providers, necessarily process certain information
            to transmit messages and operate the service. Information may also
            be disclosed when required by law.
          </p>

          <p>
            For additional details, see the Hunt Privacy Policy:<br />
            <a href="/hunt/privacy/">https://keesingai.com/hunt/privacy/</a>
          </p>

          <h2>12. No Guarantee of Availability</h2>

          <p>
            The Hunt is provided on an experimental, “as available” basis.
          </p>

          <p>
            The operator does not guarantee that the Hunt will operate without
            interruption or error or that every clue, response, location
            calculation, or other piece of information will be accurate or
            available.
          </p>

          <p>
            The operator may modify, suspend, or discontinue the Hunt or any
            portion of it at any time.
          </p>

          <h2>13. Changes to These Terms</h2>

          <p>
            These Terms may be updated as the Hunt or the technology used to
            provide it changes.
          </p>

          <p>
            The current version of the Terms will be made available on the Hunt
            website. The “Last updated” date above identifies the current
            version.
          </p>

          <p>
            If a material change affects participants' rights or the way
            personal information is handled, participants may be required to
            accept updated Terms before continuing to participate.
          </p>

          <h2>14. Acceptance of Terms</h2>

          <p>
            By texting JOIN, the Enrolling Adult confirms that they are at least
            18 years old and that they have read and agree to these Terms and
            the Hunt Privacy Policy.
          </p>

          <p>
            The Enrolling Adult also acknowledges the safety considerations and
            risks described in these Terms and accepts responsibility for their
            own actions and decisions and for providing appropriate supervision
            of minors participating on their team.
          </p>

          <h2>15. Contact</h2>

          <p>
            Questions about the Hunt or these Terms and Conditions may be
            directed to:
          </p>

          <address>
            Ron Keesing, Sole Proprietor<br />
            <a href="mailto:ron@keesingai.com">ron@keesingai.com</a>
          </address>
        </div>
      </article>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    max-width: 920px;
    padding-top: clamp(3.5rem, 6vw, 5.5rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(5rem, 9vw, 8rem);
  }

  .legal-header {
    padding-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .legal-header h1 {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.25rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .last-updated {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .legal-content {
    max-width: 780px;
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.35vw, 1.1rem);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .legal-content h2 {
    margin: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.75rem) 0 1rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .legal-content p {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
  }

  .legal-content ul {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
  }

  .legal-content li + li {
    margin-top: 0.45rem;
  }

  .legal-content strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .legal-content address {
    font-style: normal;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .legal-content a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2rem;
  }

  .legal-content a:hover,
  .legal-content a:focus-visible {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
</style>
